{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1756,1815p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d10b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc; sed -n '2074,2128p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d10b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc; sed -n '2144,2175p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d10b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- collect-inbox\n  \"Select reply-first, retaining the complete attributed record before dispatch.\n   A selected but unretained observation remains reproducible at its position.\"\n  [state]\n  (let [state (reduce dispatch-receipt state (get-in state [:inbox :control]))\n        state (-> state (assoc-in [:inbox :control] []) (dissoc :inbox-unavailable? :inbox-refused?))]\n    (loop [state state lane :reply]\n      (let [descriptor (get-in state [:seams (get inbox/lanes lane)])\n            position (get-in state [:inbox :positions lane])\n            selection (try\n                        (when (and (contains? (get-in state [:inbox :identities]) lane)\n                                   (not (inbox/same-data? (:identity descriptor)\n                                                          (get-in state [:inbox :identities lane]))))\n                          (throw (ex-info \"Changed holder inbox identity\" {::inbox/refusal :inbox-identity})))\n                        {:answer (inbox/read-at descriptor position)}\n                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) failure\n                          (if-some [reason (::inbox/refusal (ex-data failure))]\n                            {:refusal reason}\n                            (throw failure))))\n            answer (:answer selection)]\n        (if-some [reason (:refusal selection)]\n          (-> state\n              (assoc :inbox-unavailable? true :inbox-refused? true)\n              (unsatisfied reason {:yin.k/lane lane}))\n          (case (:status answer)\n            :empty (if (= :reply lane) (recur state :outcome) state)\n            :unavailable (-> state\n                             (assoc :inbox-unavailable? true)\n                             (unsatisfied :inbox-unavailable {:yin.k/lane lane}))\n            :record\n            (let [receipt (cond-> {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/inbox\n                                   :yin.k/lane lane :yin.k/identity (:identity descriptor)\n                                   :yin.k/position position :yin.k/author (:author answer)\n                                   :yin.k/record (:record answer)}\n                            (run-binding state) (assoc :yin.k/binding (run-binding state)))]\n              (journal! state receipt)\n              (recur (dispatch-receipt (-> state\n                                           (update-in [:inbox :positions lane] inc)\n                                           (assoc-in [:inbox :identities lane] (:identity descriptor))) receipt)\n                     :reply))))))))\n\n\n(defn- drain-control\n  [state]\n  (collect-inbox state))\n\n\n(defn- step-proposing\n  [state]\n  (let [state (drain-control state)]\n    (if (:inbox-unavailable? state)\n      state\n      (let [records (read-ledger! state)]\n        (if (nil? records)\n          (unsatisfied state :no-arbitration {:dao.stream/identity (:arbitration state)})\n          (let [arbitration (:arbitration state)\n                own-records (vec (mine arbitration records))\n                defect (history-defect own-records)\n                grants (filterv #(contains? (:sent-proposals state) (:dao.lease/proposal %))\n                                (grants-to arbitration (:me state) (:occurrence state) records))]\n\n(defn- step-active-held\n  \"Share binding validation and tenure between control and program scheduling.\n   Only program scheduling applies retained results or prepares an export.\"\n  [state mode]\n  (let [state (if (or (= :program mode) (nil? (:lease state))) state (collect-inbox state))]\n    (cond\n      (:inbox-refused? state) state\n      (= :releasing (:phase state)) state\n      (nil? (:lease state)) state\n      (and (:stopped? state) (nil? (get-in state [:exit :address])))\n      (end-run state :stopped {:dao.lease/lease (:lease state)})\n      (exit-settled? state)\n      (if (= :program mode) state (step-exiting state))\n      :else\n      (let [{checked :state projection :projection} (binding-check state)]\n        (if-not projection\n          checked\n          (let [drained (drain (dissoc checked :program-suspended?)\n                               (if (= :control mode) :control-buffered :program))]\n            (cond\n              (= :releasing (:phase drained)) (dissoc drained :run-end)\n              (:program-suspended? drained) (dissoc drained :program-suspended?)\n              (:run-end drained) (end-run (dissoc drained :run-end)\n                                          (get-in drained [:run-end :cause])\n                                          (dissoc (:run-end drained) :cause))\n              (:inbox-unavailable? drained) drained\n              :else\n              (let [reading (clock drained)\n                    _ (require-tenure! drained)\n                    [renewed holder] (if (= :program mode)\n                                       [drained (:holder drained)]\n                                       (renew drained (:holder drained) reading))\n                    state (assoc renewed :holder holder)\n                    armed? (some? (:exit state))\n                    preparing? (nil? (get-in state [:exit :address]))]\n                (cond\n                  (and armed?\n                       (or (and (= :control mode) preparing?)\n                           (and (= :program mode) (not preparing?)))) state\n                  armed? (drain (step-exit-body state projection) mode)\n                  (or (= :control mode) (= :activating (:phase state)))\n                  (with-status state :yin.k/ok\n                    {:yin.k/occurrence (:occurrence state) :dao.lease/lease (:lease state)})\n                  :else (cycle-result (drain (run-cycle state) mode)))))))))))\n\n\n(defn- step-active\n  \"The held step under the catch: every seam the cycle runs through\n   answers an outcome and never throws (the seam contract of\n   `initial`), so a throw here is the cycle's own -- a tenure guard or\n   a program effect -- and it ends the run.  An uncertain journal\n   append is none of these: it unwinds untouched, and `step` stalls\n   everything on it.\"\n  [state mode]\n(defn- step-releasing\n  \"A pending release is retried with the identical request until\n   authenticated carriage is acknowledged, whose acknowledgment is\n   journaled.  A release a restarted holder owes (:re-propose?)\n   re-enters as a candidate once it has left, instead of answering the\n   failure the dead run died with.\"\n  [state]\n  (let [state (drain-control state)\n        release (:release state)]\n    (if (:inbox-refused? state)\n      state\n      (if (true? (:carried release))\n        (if (and (:re-propose? release) (not (:stopped? state)))\n          (-> state\n              (dissoc :release :holder :evidence)\n              (assoc :phase :proposing :proposal nil)\n              (with-status :yin.k/awaiting-grant\n                {:yin.k/occurrence (:occurrence state)}))\n          (-> state\n              (assoc :phase :failed)\n              (update :detail assoc :dao.lease/released true)))\n        (release! state (:lease release))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Validate: the D7 pipeline with zero side effects\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- step-validating\n  [state]\n  (let [r (handoff/resume-task\n            (assoc (:receiver state)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-07 15:08:11 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-07 22:08:11 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n**Ruling: CHANGES. Neither lane’s `:unavailable` answer, by itself, stops renewal or cleanup. It suspends program progress and new activation.** Finding 2 identifies a liveness defect my sign-off missed; amend that sign-off accordingly.\n\n1. **Outcome lane unavailable:** continue custody control progress, including renewal, while complete authenticated ledger evidence confirms the same binding and `lease/holding?` remains true. Continue handling available control replies. Do not execute, replay, apply program results, prepare exports or activate a grant until inbox availability is restored. Keep the unavailable source position unchanged and retain queued observations. Missing program-result history must not prevent maintaining otherwise valid custody.\n\n2. **Reply lane unavailable:** a currently valid holder **sends due renewals and retries its existing renewal request unchanged**, with the existing durable intent/attempt brackets. It cannot credit those attempts as successful renewals: inbound `:ok` is not authenticated carriage. Preserve the original pending request ID and pre-send reading; do not advance the renewal counter, refresh the local bound or manufacture an acknowledgment. If replies recover while the holder still holds, process the retained, authenticated carriage under the existing before-and-after tenure checks. If they recover after the local bound, the acknowledgment cannot revive that run—even if the authority accepted the renewal earlier. Complete ledger evidence remains necessary for scheduling renewal; inbox availability does not waive binding validation.\n\n   Preserve reply-first inbox selection: an unavailable reply position may end that tick’s inbox scan without consuming later positions or the outcome lane. The independent custody control work must still proceed. No new merge-order rule is needed.\n\n3. **At the bound:** inbox unavailability must not bypass expiry handling. End the run once, gate the machine `:ended`, emit the existing run-end diagnostic, and establish the durable cleanup-release intent before attempting its send. Retry that same release until authenticated carriage is established, even while either inbox remains unavailable. Release is cleanup and does not require continued holding. An unavailable reply lane leaves the release unacknowledged and owed; it does not justify declaring it complete. The bounded shutdown drain may end with that durable obligation pending, and reopening must recover it. A journal append of uncertain acceptance remains a hard stall: reconcile it before any further send.\n\nD15a must distinguish **inbox availability obstruction** from **journal uncertainty or malformed/conflicting inbox evidence**. In `step-active-held`, the current `(:inbox-unavailable? drained) drained` branch precedes `renew` and must change: valid control renewal and established control brackets proceed, but every route into program work—including combined `step`—remains blocked. Preserve the unavailable diagnostic instead of overwriting it with `:yin.k/ok`; clear the obstruction only after a subsequent successful inbox scan. Existing report/release/offer prerequisites remain mandatory—unavailability cannot invent missing evidence or completion. `owed-control-write?` must remain true for an eligible pending renewal or release despite inbox unavailability; unavailable history alone is not an owed write.\n\nPin four regressions on each host: **(a)** unavailable outcomes with successful renewal carriage and zero program progress; **(b)** unavailable replies with repeated identical renewal attempts and no local bound extension; **(c)** reply recovery before versus after the bound, proving only the former can credit renewal; **(d)** persistent unavailability through expiry and a full release stream, proving one run-end, durable release retries, restart recovery and no activation. Include combined `step` as well as split scheduling.\n\nRead-only review; no files edited or suites run."}}
